From e02c73bcbe070f152d5280471c22b761f93bfedd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skippy contributors <ci@skippy.local>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:03:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 55/55] tests: time row-list attention over a host-pinned KV
 cache

With GGML_CUDA_INTEGRATED=1 and the cache in pinned host memory, a GB10
decode step that holds two or more sequences took 56-62 ms of GPU time
where device memory took 22.6 ms, while one sequence took 17 ms either
way. One sequence's rows are one contiguous run; several sequences read
through row lists with a run per row.

--kv-memory device|host|both places K and V in the device's buffer type,
in its pinned host buffer type, or measures both, so dense and row-list
attention can be timed alone against each placement.
---
 tests/test-flash-attn-rows-perf.cpp | 65 ++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test-flash-attn-rows-perf.cpp b/tests/test-flash-attn-rows-perf.cpp
index fd3179a06..4262c4cbb 100644
--- a/tests/test-flash-attn-rows-perf.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-flash-attn-rows-perf.cpp
@@ -4,7 +4,10 @@
